Atlas II proved the transformation of `christoffel` and `ricciOf` only. Here the missing Einstein–Maxwell
pieces are proved from the registered definitions:

* `raise2_transform`: `F^{ab}` is a contravariant 2-tensor; `fieldSq_transform`, `ricciScalar_transform`:
  scalars; `emStress_transform`, `einsteinMaxwell_transform`: covariant 2-tensors (4D);
* `maxwellDiv_transform`: `J^b = Σ_q K^b_q J_V^q(Φ)` (a vector) — the second-derivative terms of `Φ`
  cancel between `∂_a F^{ab}` and the inhomogeneous Christoffel term;
* `faradayCyclic_transform`: `H_{abc} = Σ J^e_a J^p_b J^q_c H_V,epq(Φ)` (a covariant 3-tensor) — uses the
  symmetry of second derivatives of `Φ` and the antisymmetry of `FV`;
* `EinsteinMaxwellCertificate.transport`: a full certificate pulls back along a coordinate change.

The three laws are different (vector, 2-tensor, 3-tensor); none is assumed. -/

